PKGBUILD_MODEL(3)

# NAME

pkgbuild_model - package-build values and identity domains

# DESCRIPTION

A *build_input* binds one exact source-owned build or check requirement to the
matching *libpkgresolve* requirement edge and selected package. It does not
claim that a filesystem tree has been materialized.

An *environment_policy* fixes C.UTF-8, UTC, denied network access, and an
isolated home while sealing parallelism, umask, and optional SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH.
Ambient name/value maps are not build authority.

A *payload_manifest* is an ordered complete set of canonical package objects.
It retains path, type, mode, numeric ownership, size, timestamp, regular-content
digest, symbolic-link target, hard-link topology, and device numbers.

A *sealed_artifact* records encoding, compression, exact byte count, and
complete SHA-256. Its pathname is not part of the value.

All identities use domain-separated canonical SHA-256 records.

# SEE ALSO

*libpkgbuild*(3), *pkgbuild_request*(3), *pkgbuild_result*(3)
